@startuml digital-product-stress-events
title Correlated event-based purchase and activation audit
autonumber
actor "Orchestrating client" as client
queue "Event broker" as bus
participant "Purchase worker" as worker
participant "HTTP fulfilment services" as http
participant "Activation audit worker" as audit
participant "Coordinator state API" as state
note over client,audit: Start consumers before publication; correlate by purchaseId.\nStable eventId deduplicates a publication.
client ->> bus: PurchaseRequested (purchase data, correlationId, eventId)
bus ->> worker: Matching PurchaseRequested
worker -> http: Invoke supplied fulfil-item workflow
http --> worker: Workflow-control continuation (not an HTTP response)
worker -> state: GET /purchases/{purchaseId}
state --> worker: Confirmed READY and scoped licenseId
worker ->> bus: PurchaseCompleted (READY, purchaseId, licenseId)
bus ->> client: Matching PurchaseCompleted
alt Receive times out or fails criteria
  loop At most two receive retries, 0.5s delay; each wait up to 12s
    bus ->> client: Matching completion if available
  end
  client -> state: One-way polling fallback; do not republish purchase command
  state --> client: READY / PENDING / FAILED
else READY event received and verified
  client ->> bus: ActivationReported (actual ACTIVATED or FAILED outcome)
  bus ->> audit: Matching ActivationReported
  audit -> state: POST /purchases/{purchaseId}/activation-events
  state --> audit: 204 (report received)
  audit ->> bus: AuditRecorded (RECORDED, original activation eventId)
  bus ->> client: Matching AuditRecorded
  note over client,state: Final read joins await-ready and await-audit.
  client -> state: GET /purchases/{purchaseId}
  state --> client: Authoritative READY state and matching licenseId
end
note over client,bus: Sending does not assert broker acknowledgment or delivery.\nUnrelated correlation IDs do not complete a receive step.
note over client,audit: RECORDED acknowledges the report; it does not turn FAILED activation into success.
@enduml
